  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUPP TZ HEALTH SECT STRATEGIC PLAN V TO DELIVER PRIMARY HEALTHCARE SERV TOWARD</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Health Basket Fund (HBF) is a pooled funding mechanism that works through national systems to support delivery of primary health care services, including reproductive, maternal, new-born, and child health, for poor and under-served populations. It remains the largest and most reliable source of funding for primary healthcare facilities in Tanzania. The majority of the HBF resources (90%) are channelled directly to the bank accounts of over 6,780 primary health facilities (local dispensaries, health centres and district hospitals) to provide primary healthcare. A remaining proportion of the funds (10%) is allocated to the Ministry of Health and the President&#x2019;s office, Regional Administration and Local Government (PORALG) for management, quality assurance and accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
